            "text": "{\"description\":\"The visible stone face is divided into horizontal bands with relief carvings: at the top are three large arch-topped shapes, below them are incised repeated strokes and animal or birdlike figures. In the lower portion there is a large elongated birdlike head and neck with a small circular eye-like detail, plus other worn linear forms and partial limbs or bodies.\",\"avian\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"A clear birdlike head with a curved beak and long neck is carved near the lower left of the main surface; another birdlike form with outstretched body is visible in the middle band.\",\"box\":[0.18,0.76,0.39,0.98]},\"large_face\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"No large human face with facial features is visible on the main carved surface; the visible heads are birdlike or too worn/partial.\",\"box\":null},\"scorpion\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"I do not see a carved scorpion with multiple legs or a segmented upturned tail on the visible surface.\",\"box\":null},\"round_motif\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"The only distinct small round mark appears to be an eye on the lower birdlike head, which is excluded; no separate circular motif is visible.\",\"box\":null},\"three_arches\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"Across the top band there are three repeated arch-topped forms arranged side by side.\",\"box\":[0.08,0.03,0.75,0.22]},\"limitations\":\"Strong sunlight and shadows, surface wear, broken edges, and overlapping relief lines make some details difficult to read.\"}",
